    "explanation": "Because finger flexor/extensor tendons cross both the wrist and finger joints with a relatively fixed excursion, passive wrist extension tensions the flexor tendons (producing passive finger flexion), and passive wrist flexion has the opposite effect—a principle sometimes used functionally in patients with certain hand paralysis (e.g., some tetraplegic patients)."
