    "explanation": "Arthrogenic muscle inhibition describes a reflex-mediated reduction in muscle activation capacity secondary to joint pathology (e.g., effusion, injury), which can persist despite the muscle itself remaining structurally and neurologically intact, and is a key rationale for using NMES to help overcome this inhibition."
